# fsync durability test image: persistprobe on a real-disk KRFFS.
#
# Built into a partitioned disk by mkdisk.sh and booted twice against one scratch
# copy with rach2.fsdisk + rach2.rescue. The first boot writes and fsyncs
# /persist.txt; the second reads it back, proving fsync pushed the write through
# the page cache to the disk.
file 0755 /persistprobe build/tests/persistprobe
